      "code": "tb_font_info->glyph_to_cache_index.reserve(word->getLength());",
      "role": "source",
      "note": "reserve() only allocates capacity, it does not change size(); glyph_to_cache_index.size() remains 0 even though capacity is now word->getLength(), so the vector is still logically empty while attacker-controlled word length flows in as the intended element count."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "file": "poppler/cpp/poppler-page.cpp",
      "function": "page::text_list",
      "line": 478,
      "var": "tb_font_info->glyph_to_cache_index[j]",
      "code": "tb_font_info->glyph_to_cache_index[j] = -1;",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "note": "direct operator[] write is used instead of push_back/resize, so glyph_to_cache_index.size() never grows past 0 even though j iterates up to word->getLength()-1; the safety obligation that j < glyph_to_cache_index.size() before indexed write is violated because reserve() never increased size()."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "file": "poppler/cpp/poppler-page.cpp",
